## 🔄 State Management - Riverpod Streaming Architecture

### 🎯 Core State Management Principles
- **All data sources use streams** for reactive updates
- **Repository pattern** with abstract interfaces for easy backend swapping  
- **AsyncValue handling** throughout with proper loading/error states
- **Dependency injection** via Riverpod providers
- **No runtime provider initialization** - use Family providers for context-dependent state

### Current Implementation Pattern
```dart
// Repository provider - swap storage implementations easily
@riverpod
GameRepository gameRepository(Ref ref) {
  final storageService = ref.read(storageServiceProvider);
  final repository = DriftGameRepository(storageService);
  ref.onDispose(() => repository.dispose());
  return repository;
}

// Streaming data provider
@riverpod
Stream<List<GameItem>> gamesStream(Ref ref) {
  final repository = ref.watch(gameRepositoryProvider);
  return repository.watchGames();
}

// Current state provider for UI consumption
@riverpod
class GameList extends _$GameList {
  @override
  List<GameItem> build() {
    final gamesAsync = ref.watch(gamesStreamProvider);
    return gamesAsync.when(
      data: (games) => games,
      loading: () => [],
      error: (error, stack) => [],
    );
  }

  // CRUD operations
  Future<void> createGame({...}) async { /* implementation */ }
  Future<void> updateGame(GameItem updatedGame) async { /* implementation */ }
  Future<void> removeGame(GameId gameId) async { /* implementation */ }
}

// Derived providers - automatically update when base data changes
@riverpod
List<GameItem> gamesByStatus(Ref ref, GameStatus status) {
  final games = ref.watch(gameListProvider);
  return games.where((game) => game.status == status).toList();
}
```

### 🎯 Family Provider Rules (Critical for Context-Dependent State)
- **Always use Family** for screen-specific state instead of runtime initialization
- **Create context classes** with proper `==` and `hashCode` implementation
- **Initialize context in initState()** not provider state
- **Use simple `pump()`** in tests instead of `pumpAndSettle()`

```dart
// Context class for Family parameters
class GameEditContext {
  final bool isAddMode;
  final GameItem? game;

  const GameEditContext({required this.isAddMode, this.game});

  @override
  bool operator ==(Object other) => 
    identical(this, other) ||
    other is GameEditContext &&
    isAddMode == other.isAddMode &&
    game == other.game;

  @override
  int get hashCode => Object.hash(isAddMode, game);
}

// Family provider - eliminates initialization issues
@riverpod
class GameEditState extends _$GameEditState {
  @override
  GameEditFormState build(GameEditContext context) {
    if (context.isAddMode) {
      return const GameEditFormState.empty();
    } else {
      return GameEditFormState.fromGame(context.game!);
    }
  }
}
```

