## 🎨 Styling Architecture - Critical Android 13 Compatibility

### 🚨 **NEVER** Rely on Material Design Defaults
**CRITICAL RULE**: Android 13 and older versions handle Material Design theming differently, causing text and UI elements to become invisible. Always use **explicit colour and style declarations**.

#### ❌ **FORBIDDEN PATTERNS** - These cause Android 13 invisibility:
```dart
// NEVER use theme-based styling
Text('Hello', style: Theme.of(context).textTheme.bodyMedium)
Container(color: Theme.of(context).cardColor)
Card(child: Text('Hello')) // Background colour undefined

// NEVER use TextStyle without explicit colours
Text('Hello', style: TextStyle(fontSize: 16)) // No colour = invisible text
```

#### ✅ **REQUIRED PATTERNS** - Always use explicit styling:
```dart
// ALWAYS use explicit colours from AppColors
Text('Hello', style: TextStyle(
  fontSize: 16,
  color: AppColors.primaryText, // Explicit colour required
  fontWeight: FontWeight.w500,
))

// ALWAYS specify Card colours explicitly
Card(
  color: Colors.white, // Explicit background
  child: Text('Hello', style: TextStyle(color: AppColors.primaryText)),
)

// ALWAYS use explicit button styling
ElevatedButton(
  onPressed: onPressed,
  style: ElevatedButton.styleFrom(
    backgroundColor: AppColors.primaryPurple,
    foregroundColor: Colors.white,
    disabledBackgroundColor: Colors.grey[300],
    disabledForegroundColor: Colors.grey[600],
  ),
  child: Text('Click'),
)
```

### Current Styling Implementation
```dart
// Centralised styling in lib/styles/
import 'package:chkpnt/styles/game_card_styles.dart';
import 'package:chkpnt/styles/global_styles.dart';

